<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml" xmlns:h="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" version="1.0" name="ReviewSession" initial="idle"><metadata><h:section id="documentation"><h:h2>ReviewSession — actor contract</h:h2><h:p><h:strong>Actor invariant: </h:strong>Local IndexedDB is authoritative for V1; no auth server or server event log required.</h:p><h:p><h:strong>Specification: </h:strong>ACT-SESSION in <h:a href="../system.xml">system.xml</h:a>. These comments use XHTML namespace h: and are not executable SCXML actions.</h:p><h:h3>I/O contracts invoked by this actor</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-AUTH">review.auth.authorize</h:a> — AuthorizeRequest → AuthorizeResult | Fault; external-write, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-001, FL-002; requirements: REQ-001, REQ-003, REQ-059</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-SESSION-RESUME">review.session.resume</h:a> — ResumeRequest → ResumeResult | Fault; read, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-016, FL-017; requirements: REQ-011, REQ-055, REQ-057, REQ-069</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-SNAPSHOT-SAVE">review.cache.snapshot</h:a> — SnapshotSaveRequest → SnapshotSaveResult | Fault; local-write, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-016; requirements: REQ-055, REQ-011</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-SNAPSHOT-LOAD">review.cache.restore</h:a> — SnapshotLoadRequest → SnapshotLoadResult | Fault; read, never, 10000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-016; requirements: REQ-055, REQ-011</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-CRED-TEST">review.credentials.test</h:a> — CredentialTestRequest → CredentialTestResult | Fault; external-write, never, 12000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-024, FL-048; requirements: REQ-092, REQ-093</h:li><h:li><h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-CRED-FORGET">review.credentials.forget</h:a> — CredentialForgetRequest → CredentialForgetResult | Fault; local-write, never, 12000 ms max. <h:a href="../io-messages.xsd">XSD</h:a>; flows: FL-048; requirements: REQ-093, REQ-101</h:li></h:ul></h:section></metadata><state id="idle">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-idle"><h:h3>State: idle</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>widget.boot</h:code> → ready</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="widget.boot" target="ready"/>
  </state>
  <state id="authenticating">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-authenticating"><h:h3>State: authenticating</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>auth.succeeded</h:code> → ready<h:a href="../io-processors.xml#IO-AUTH"> [typed result: IO-AUTH]</h:a></h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="auth.succeeded" target="ready"/>
  </state>
  <state id="ready">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-ready"><h:h3>State: ready</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>review.start</h:code> → active</h:li><h:li><h:code>review.resume</h:code> → active</h:li><h:li><h:code>credentials.configure</h:code> → ready</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="review.start" target="active"/>
    <transition event="review.resume" target="active"/>
    <transition event="credentials.configure" target="ready"/>
  </state>
  <state id="active">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-active"><h:h3>State: active</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>network.offline</h:code> → offline</h:li><h:li><h:code>page.changed</h:code> → active</h:li><h:li><h:code>observation.saved</h:code> → active</h:li><h:li><h:code>review.close</h:code> → closing</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="network.offline" target="offline"/>
    <transition event="page.changed" target="active"/>
    <transition event="observation.saved" target="active"/>
    <transition event="review.close" target="closing"/>
  </state>
  <state id="offline">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-offline"><h:h3>State: offline</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>network.online</h:code> → active</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="network.online" target="active"/>
  </state>
  <state id="closing">
    <metadata><h:section id="state-closing"><h:h3>State: closing</h:h3><h:ul><h:li><h:code>review.closed</h:code> → closed</h:li></h:ul><h:p>I/O result events are delivered only after the corresponding processor returns a schema-valid result. On fault, apply the operation-specific failureHandling contract, never a silent success transition.</h:p></h:section></metadata><transition event="review.closed" target="closed"/>
  </state>
  <state id="closed"><metadata><h:section id="state-closed"><h:h3>State: closed</h:h3><h:p>No outgoing transitions in this version. This state is terminal until the host ends or restores the actor.</h:p></h:section></metadata></state>
</scxml>
